# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do you see advantages to amplitude encoding over basis encoding? If so, explain.\n"
msgstr "Apakah kamu melihat keuntungan amplitude encoding dibanding basis encoding? Kalau iya, jelaskan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There may be several answers. One answer is that, given the fixed ordering of the basis states, this amplitude encoding preserves the order of the numbers encoded. It will often also be encoded more densely.\n"
msgstr "Mungkin ada beberapa jawaban. Salah satu jawabannya adalah bahwa, mengingat urutan basis state yang tetap, amplitude encoding ini mempertahankan urutan angka yang di-encode. Ini juga sering di-encode lebih padat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A benefit of amplitude encoding is that only $\\log_2(N)$ qubits are required for an $N$-dimensional ($N$-feature) data vector $\\vec{x}\\rightarrow|\\vec{x}\\rangle$. However, amplitude encoding is generally an inefficient procedure that requires arbitrary state preparation, which is exponential in the number of CNOT gates. Stated differently, the state preparation has a polynomial runtime complexity of $\\mathcal O(N)$ in the number of dimensions, where $N = 2^n$, and $n$ is the number of qubits. Amplitude encoding “provides an exponential saving in space at the cost of an exponential increase in time”[\\[3\\]](#references); however, runtime increases to $\\mathcal O(\\log N)$ are achievable in certain cases[\\[4\\]](#references). For an end-to-end quantum speedup, the data loading runtime complexity needs to be considered.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Keuntungan dari amplitude encoding adalah bahwa hanya $\\log_2(N)$ qubit yang diperlukan untuk vektor data $N$-dimensi ($N$-fitur) $\\vec{x}\\rightarrow|\\vec{x}\\rangle$. Namun, amplitude encoding pada umumnya adalah prosedur yang tidak efisien yang memerlukan persiapan state sembarang, yang bersifat eksponensial dalam jumlah Gate CNOT. Dengan kata lain, persiapan state memiliki kompleksitas runtime polinomial $\\mathcal O(N)$ dalam jumlah dimensi, di mana $N = 2^n$, dan $n$ adalah jumlah qubit. Amplitude encoding \"memberikan penghematan eksponensial dalam ruang dengan biaya peningkatan eksponensial dalam waktu\"[\\[3\\]](#references); namun, peningkatan runtime menjadi $\\mathcal O(\\log N)$ dapat dicapai dalam kasus tertentu[\\[4\\]](#references). Untuk quantum speedup end-to-end, kompleksitas runtime loading data perlu dipertimbangkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle encoding {#angle-encoding}"
msgstr "Angle encoding {#angle-encoding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle encoding is of interest in many QML models using Pauli feature maps such as quantum support vector machines (QSVMs) and variational quantum circuits (VQCs), among others. Angle encoding is closely related to phase encoding and dense angle encoding which are presented below. Here we will use \"angle encoding\" to refer to a rotation in $\\theta$, that is, a rotation away from the $z$ axis accomplished for example by an $R_X$ gate or an $R_Y$ gate[\\[1,3\\]](#references). Really, one can encode data in *any* rotation or combination of rotations. But $R_Y$ is common in the literature, so we emphasize it here.\n"
msgstr "Angle encoding menarik perhatian dalam banyak model QML yang menggunakan Pauli feature map seperti quantum support vector machine (QSVM) dan variational quantum circuit (VQC), di antara yang lain. Angle encoding erat kaitannya dengan phase encoding dan dense angle encoding yang disajikan di bawah. Di sini kami akan menggunakan \"angle encoding\" untuk merujuk pada rotasi dalam $\\theta$, yaitu rotasi menjauhi sumbu $z$ yang dilakukan misalnya oleh Gate $R_X$ atau Gate $R_Y$[\\[1,3\\]](#references). Sebenarnya, data bisa di-encode dalam *rotasi manapun* atau kombinasi rotasi. Tapi $R_Y$ umum dalam literatur, jadi kami menekankannya di sini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When applied to a single qubit, angle encoding imparts a Y-axis rotation proportional to the data value. Consider the encoding of a single ($k^\\text{th}$)feature from the $j^\\text{th}$ data vector in a dataset, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k$:\n"
msgstr "Ketika diterapkan pada satu qubit, angle encoding memberikan rotasi sumbu Y yang proporsional dengan nilai data. Pertimbangkan encoding satu fitur ke-$k$ dari vektor data ke-$j$ dalam dataset, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = R_Y(\\theta=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle = \\textstyle\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle + \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = R_Y(\\theta=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle = \\textstyle\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle + \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, angle encoding can be performed using $R_X(\\theta)$ gates, although the encoded state would have a complex relative phase compared to $R_Y(\\theta)$.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif, angle encoding bisa dilakukan menggunakan Gate $R_X(\\theta)$, meskipun state yang di-encode akan memiliki fase relatif kompleks dibandingkan dengan $R_Y(\\theta)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Angle encoding is different from the previous two methods discussed in several ways. In angle encoding:\n"
"- Each feature value is mapped to a corresponding qubit, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$, leaving the qubits in a product state.\n"
"- One numerical value is encoded at a time, rather than a whole set of features from a data point.\n"
"- $n$ qubits are required for $N$ data features, where $n\\leq N$. Often equality holds, here. We'll see how $n<N$ is possible in the next few sections.\n"
"- The resulting circuit is a constant depth (typically the depth is 1 prior to transpilation).\n"
msgstr ""
"Angle encoding berbeda dari dua metode sebelumnya yang dibahas dalam beberapa hal. Dalam angle encoding:\n"
"- Setiap nilai fitur dipetakan ke qubit yang sesuai, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$, meninggalkan qubit dalam product state.\n"
"- Satu nilai numerik di-encode dalam satu waktu, bukan seluruh set fitur dari satu titik data.\n"
"- $n$ qubit diperlukan untuk $N$ fitur data, di mana $n\\leq N$. Sering kali kesetaraan berlaku di sini. Kita akan melihat bagaimana $n<N$ bisa terjadi di beberapa bagian berikutnya.\n"
"- Circuit kuantum yang dihasilkan memiliki kedalaman konstan (biasanya kedalaman 1 sebelum transpilasi).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constant depth quantum circuit makes it particularly amenable to current quantum hardware. One additional feature of encoding our data using $\\theta$ (and specifically, our choice to use Y-axis angle encoding) is that it creates real-valued quantum states that can be useful for certain applications. For Y-axis rotation, data is mapped with a Y-axis rotation gate $R_Y(\\theta)$ by a real-valued angle $\\theta \\in (0, 2\\pi]$ ([Qiskit RYGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RYGate)). As with phase encoding (see below), we recommend that you rescale data so that $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$, preventing information loss and other unwanted effects.\n"
msgstr "Circuit kuantum kedalaman konstan membuatnya sangat cocok untuk hardware kuantum saat ini. Satu fitur tambahan dari encoding data menggunakan $\\theta$ (dan khususnya, pilihan kita untuk menggunakan Y-axis angle encoding) adalah bahwa ia menciptakan state kuantum bernilai real yang bisa berguna untuk aplikasi tertentu. Untuk rotasi sumbu Y, data dipetakan dengan Gate rotasi sumbu Y $R_Y(\\theta)$ dengan sudut bernilai real $\\theta \\in (0, 2\\pi]$ ([Qiskit RYGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RYGate)). Seperti dengan phase encoding (lihat di bawah), kami menyarankan agar kamu mengubah skala data sehingga $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$, mencegah kehilangan informasi dan efek yang tidak diinginkan lainnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following Qiskit code rotates a single qubit from an initial state $|0\\rangle$ to encode a data value $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"
msgstr "Kode Qiskit berikut merotasi satu qubit dari state awal $|0\\rangle$ untuk meng-encode nilai data $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will define a function to visualize the action on the state vector. The details of the function definition are not important, but the ability to visualize the state vectors and their changes is important.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mendefinisikan fungsi untuk memvisualisasikan aksi pada vektor state. Detail definisi fungsi tidak penting, tapi kemampuan untuk memvisualisasikan vektor state dan perubahannya itu penting.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/666700f7-7798-43ce-a8ca-d91e48adda4f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/666700f7-7798-43ce-a8ca-d91e48adda4f-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That was just a single feature of a single data vector. When encoding $N$ features into the rotation angles of $n$ qubits, say for the $j^\\text{th}$ data vector $\\vec{x}^{(j)} = (x_1,...,x_N),$ the encoded product state will look like this:\n"
msgstr "Itu baru satu fitur dari satu vektor data. Ketika meng-encode $N$ fitur ke dalam sudut rotasi dari $n$ qubit, misalnya untuk vektor data ke-$j$ $\\vec{x}^{(j)} = (x_1,...,x_N),$ product state yang di-encode akan terlihat seperti ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} \\cos(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle + \\sin(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} \\cos(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle + \\sin(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We note that this is equivalent to\n"
msgstr "Kita perhatikan bahwa ini ekuivalen dengan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} R_Y(2\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} R_Y(2\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Cek pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encode the data vector $\\vec{x} = (0, \\pi/4, \\pi/2)$ using angle encoding, as described above.\n"
msgstr "Encode vektor data $\\vec{x} = (0, \\pi/4, \\pi/2)$ menggunakan angle encoding, seperti yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"Output of the previous code cell\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/checkin4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"Output of the previous code cell\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/checkin4.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using angle encoding as described above, how many qubits are required to encode 5 features?\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan angle encoding seperti yang dijelaskan di atas, berapa banyak qubit yang diperlukan untuk meng-encode 5 fitur?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "5\n"
msgstr "__Jawaban:__ 5\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase encoding {#phase-encoding}"
msgstr "Phase encoding {#phase-encoding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase encoding is very similar to the angle encoding described above. The phase angle of a qubit is a real-valued angle $\\phi$ about the $z$-axis from the +$x$-axis. Data are mapped with a phase rotation, $P(\\phi) = e^{i\\phi/2}R_Z(\\phi)$, where $\\phi \\in (0,2\\pi]$ (see [Qiskit PhaseGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PhaseGate) for more information). It is recommended to rescale data so that $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$. This prevents information loss and other potentially unwanted effects[\\[1,2\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Phase encoding sangat mirip dengan angle encoding yang dijelaskan di atas. Sudut fase dari sebuah qubit adalah sudut bernilai real $\\phi$ terhadap sumbu $z$ dari sumbu +$x$. Data dipetakan dengan rotasi fase, $P(\\phi) = e^{i\\phi/2}R_Z(\\phi)$, di mana $\\phi \\in (0,2\\pi]$ (lihat [Qiskit PhaseGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PhaseGate) untuk informasi lebih lanjut). Disarankan untuk mengubah skala data sehingga $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$. Ini mencegah kehilangan informasi dan efek yang berpotensi tidak diinginkan lainnya[\\[1,2\\]](#references).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is often initialized in the state $|0\\rangle$, which is an eigenstate of the phase rotation operator, meaning that the qubit state first needs to be rotated for phase encoding to be implemented. It therefore makes sense to initialize the state with a Hadamard gate: $H|0\\rangle = |+\\rangle = \\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$. Phase encoding on a single qubit means imparting a relative phase proportional to the data value:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah qubit sering diinisialisasi dalam state $|0\\rangle$, yang merupakan eigenstate dari operator rotasi fase, artinya state qubit pertama-tama perlu dirotasi agar phase encoding dapat diimplementasikan. Oleh karena itu masuk akal untuk menginisialisasi state dengan Gate Hadamard: $H|0\\rangle = |+\\rangle = \\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$. Phase encoding pada satu qubit berarti memberikan fase relatif yang proporsional dengan nilai data:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = P(\\phi=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|+\\rangle = \\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\big(|0\\rangle + e^{i\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}|1\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = P(\\phi=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|+\\rangle = \\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\big(|0\\rangle + e^{i\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}|1\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase encoding procedure maps each feature value to the phase of a corresponding qubit, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$. In total, phase encoding has a circuit depth of 2, including the Hadamard layer, which makes it an efficient encoding scheme. The phase-encoded multi-qubit state ($n$ qubits for $N=n$ features) is a product state:\n"
msgstr "Prosedur phase encoding memetakan setiap nilai fitur ke fase dari qubit yang sesuai, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$. Secara keseluruhan, phase encoding memiliki kedalaman Circuit 2, termasuk lapisan Hadamard, yang membuatnya menjadi skema encoding yang efisien. State multi-Qubit yang di-encode dengan phase ($n$ qubit untuk $N=n$ fitur) adalah product state:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes_{k=1}^{N} P_k(\\phi = \\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|+\\rangle^{\\otimes N} = {\\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^N}}} \\bigotimes_{k=1}^{N}\\big(|0\\rangle + e^{i\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}|1\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes_{k=1}^{N} P_k(\\phi = \\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|+\\rangle^{\\otimes N} = {\\textstyle\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^N}}} \\bigotimes_{k=1}^{N}\\big(|0\\rangle + e^{i\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}|1\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following Qiskit code first prepares the initial state of a single qubit by rotating it with a Hadamard gate, then rotates it again using a phase gate to encode a data feature $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"
msgstr "Kode Qiskit berikut pertama menyiapkan state awal satu qubit dengan merotasinya menggunakan Gate Hadamard, kemudian merotasinya lagi menggunakan Gate fase untuk meng-encode fitur data $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"

